        I've been playing NetHack on and off for a couple years now,
and
today I finally made my first ascension. I think my recent 9-month
hiatus from the game was good for me. (Got disillusioned for a while
after ungloriously losing a very promising valkyrie to "one more"
giant corpse and a lack of a #heimlich command... Next patch, maybe?)

        Anyway, I picked it up again shortly after New Years and this
time my
overall approach was much better. I used to get very bogged down in
the very early game until I inevitably ran into a YAAD without the
gear to prevent it. The farthest I'd gotten before this last month was
DLvl 12. So I was breaking a lot of new ground when I started running
characters last month and surviving well past the early game. While I
had a number of silly and annoying deaths, I developed good habits and
learned ways to avoid the common early game pitfalls. So at long last,
I make my first ascension with, of all characters, TimTamRan the
lawful human Archeologist.

        I ran something of a protection racket in the early game all
the way
through sokoban. My trusty kitten, Griffin, loyally defended me as I
dug around for vaults and by the time I went back up to visit Minetown
I had a sizeable collection of gold. Donated most of it to the priest.
Result: "Thy selfless generosity is deeply appreciated" and no
improvement in AC. WTF? Reread the wiki entry on donation more closely
and smacked myself for being an overachieving sucker.

        I shrugged it off, mostly because after shopping in Minetown
and
IDing my inventory with various methods I found that I had collected
no less than three magic lamps, an amulet of reflection, and a bag of
holding. Yay! Unsure at this point what kind of dragon mail I wanted,
I used one to wish for a blessed fixed +2 grayswandir and saved the
others. Soon after I found a silver sabre and raised both sabre and
twoweapon skills to expert. After spending most of the game thus far
hacking at nasties with a dwarven mattock this was a welcome
improvement. I suddenly transformed from a shy, bookish type cowering
behind my ferocious pet into a dual-wielding, undead-slaying
berserker. Fun times.

        Hoping I might get some silver dragon scales in the midgame
and save
a wish, I sicced Griffin on all the dwarves and hobbits I could find
in the mine to get some nice armor to tide me over. Got me some decent
+4 elven mithril in the end, but Griffin was somehow killed in the
process. Psh. Didn't need her anymore anwyay... But I still made a
note to use the first scroll of genocide I found on all h.

        Found a cloak of MR in the grave of one of my unfortunate
Samurai who
had experienced an embarrasing YASD. Safe from polymorph traps, I
headed down to Mines End, got my luckstone, and maxed out my luck with
ID'd gems and a white unicorn (yay for arcs!). I then decided to see
if I could give divine protection another shot with Ludios gold.
Especially with the ring of conflict I had found on DLvl 2, I felt
pretty secure against whatever Croesus' forces could throw at me.

        I cleared out the fort with minimal effort, personally
dispatching
whatever survived the raging scene of conflict. Picked up about 50k of
gold and went back to Minetown to spend about half of it on protection
- doing it right this time.

        Now with an AC of -12 and about to plunge deeper into the
dungeon, I
finally decided to use one of my other two magic lamps on some SDSM.
Pulled them out of my BoH, blessed them, rubbed them, and got a
neutral and a tame djinn out of the deal. Shook fist at RNG.

        Read some ID scrolls. Found out that I'd acquired a couple
scrolls of
genocide. Goodnight moon, goodnight humanoids, goodnight liches.

        After completing the quest, slaying medusa, and clearing out
the
castle with very little incident, I went back up to my stash with the
wand of wishing to take stock and prepare my ascension kit. I had
already acquired teleport control and teleportitis, as well as a pair
of speed boots and some GoP. I'd also found some water walking boots,
so I made a pool of water and went on a scroll-blanking, potion-
diluting binge. Used one wish on some SDSM and another on a magic
marker, did some scroll writing and ended up with the following
outfit:

a - a blessed +7 silver saber (wielded in other hand)
b - the blessed +7 Grayswandir (weapon in hand)

A - a blessed greased +5 silver dragon scale mail (being worn)
B - a blessed fireproof +5 pair of speed boots (being worn)
C - a blessed greased fireproof +5 cloak of magic resistance (being
worn)
E - a blessed greased fireproof +6 elven leather helm (being worn)
G - a blessed rustproof +5 pair of gauntlets of power (being worn)

        Quite pleased with myself, I realized I had my entire
ascension kit
with several wishes to spare. I also had a formidable arsenal of
escape items and wands. I wrote one more blessed scroll of genocide to
save for the plane of water, wished for a blessed spellbook of
identify, a wand of polymorph, and a wand of death just for fun, and
saved my last wish for a rubber chicken if I ever needed one.

        If you haven't already noticed, I was massively overprepared
for my
first ascension run. So I further overprepared by polypiling until I
had 5 amulets of lifesaving and makng sure I had dug straight lines
between the staircases on every level. THEN I descended into Gehennom.

        The realm of Moloch was actually disappointingly easy. I think
I was
spoiled by having learned magic mapping, and my weapon combo killed
nearly every denizen of the underworld with only one or two attacks.
None of the demon princes posed any kind of threat, although I had to
rubber chicken Orcus after finding out that the whole "my wand of
death is bigger than YOUR wand of death" thing didn't work out so
well.

        Zap magic mapping, slay some demons, dig some tunnels, beat
Vlad to
death with a spoon. Yawn. Finally killed Rodney and took his book. I
levelported to the vibrating square and performed the invocation,
fought my way through the Sanctum and for the first time in my many
lives, obtained the Amulet of Yendor. The run back up was fairly non
eventful. I acquired a third wand of death somewhere along the line
and just zapped Rodney every time he showed up, and with the Orb of
Detection even the malignant aura caused hardly any trouble.

        I breezed through the elemental planes with style, having
saved up
some booze and scrolls of gold detection. I Xorned my way through the
Plane of Earth, killed everything on the Plane of Air just to be
baller (did have to spend some time healing in an energy vortex,
however), and the portal on the Plane of Fire was generated just a few
steps away from where I entered. I genocided all ; as soon as I
arrived on the Plane of Water, rode around in some bubbles and then
excitedly jumped into the portal to the Astral Plane without taking my
ring of conflict off.

        Oh well, I could beat everything to death in a few hits
anyway. And I
still had about 12 charges between my two remaining wands of death.
Killed me some angels, priests, and Riders and found the lawful high
altar in the second temple I explored.

        I offered the amulet and ascended to the sound of heavenly
choirs.
Fin.

        Now what do I do?


